infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title JSON vs Protobuf on the wire
  desc Trade human-readable, self-describing text for a schema-bound binary contract
  compares
    - label JSON / REST
      children
        - label Human-readable on the wire
          desc Keys travel as UTF-8 text — readable in DevTools, curl, and logs
        - label Self-describing
          desc Schema ships with every message; no .proto needed to decode
        - label Works in the browser directly
          desc No proxy hop — any frontend can call REST/JSON
        - label Slower and larger
          desc Text parse plus key allocation; ~4-5x bigger on numeric data
    - label Protobuf / gRPC
      children
        - label 4-5x smaller, 5-10x faster parse
          desc Varint binary — no text tokenizing or key-string allocation
        - label Schema-bound binary
          desc Field numbers, not names, on the wire — opaque without the .proto
        - label Field number is a permanent contract
          desc Append-only, reserve removals, never renumber
        - label Browser cannot speak it natively
          desc Needs grpc-web plus a translating proxy such as Envoy
theme
  palette #f59e0b #6366f1
